This product includes software developed by Google LLC as part of myanmar-tools
(https://github.com/google/myanmar-tools), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0:

  * third_party/myanmar-tools/zawgyiUnicodeModel.dat, the Zawgyi detection model
  * third_party/myanmar-tools/Z2U.js and U2Z.js, the CLDR Zawgyi and Unicode
    transliteration rules
  * third_party/myanmar-tools/test, Google's test documents

These files are included unmodified. src/detector.mjs is ported from Google's
zawgyi_detector.ts and changed to expose the model's evidence for any part of a
line. src/transliterate.mjs reproduces the transliteration runner from Google's
zawgyi_converter.ts.

The benchmark sentences in bench/sentences.txt and the cases derived from them in
bench/cases.jsonl come from Burmese Wikipedia (the wikimedia/wikipedia dump
20231101.my) and are available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 License.

Some cases in test/regressions.json quote short lines from CC-100
(https://data.statmt.org/cc-100/), a web corpus drawn from Common Crawl.
